  annotation "note_1771590801121_0", anchor: "Forty-six functional filaments — the forty-seventh having been slack since before the Breach", text: "Xi counts forty-seven, calls the last one dead. The Pinnacle counts forty-six functional. Ingjeizhi — with the calm authority of something that grew the filaments from its own lattice — states the forty-seventh was singing at a register crystal carries but feathers cannot feel. Three witnesses, three states for one string: dead, slack, speaking. How extraordinary that the rashomon structure should earn itself most precisely on a question of acoustics.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771590801121_1", anchor: "the fire-core residue I'd carried from the Nightshelf runs, the taint of hoarded crystal", text: "Both civilizations named in a single breath — fire-cores from the Nightshelf depths, hoarded crystal from Aurora stockpiles — and Xi describes carrying them as contamination. The Flipper Accord's entire architecture reduced to residue on a smuggler's flippers. One people mines volcanic heat from increasingly unstable depths; the other grows light in ice over centuries. Neither survives without the other's export. Xi became criminal by moving both resources where the Accord's public text forbade, under terms its secret renegotiations had already abandoned.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771590801121_2", anchor: "A sound with no name in this cycle, or the last, or the one before", text: "Xi uses a nearly identical phrase: 'a sound that has no name in this cycle.' One cycle's reach from a mortal witness. Three cycles' reach from the spire. The convergence is uncanny — and the temporal deepening matters. During the Long Dark, the boundary between living world and ice-memory thins: the dead speak clearly, visions arrive unbidden, ice-readers lose control of abilities that suddenly reach too far. This blessing did not occur during a Long Dark. But the frequency Ingjeizhi describes — completing a circuit broken since before sapience, drawing response from ice no one has carved or named — behaves precisely as veil-thinning phenomena behave. Either the harp induced a localized thinning, or the boundary at Light Ingjeizhi was already compromised. Neither possibility appears in the custodial records.", type: :commentary, display: :full, source_anchor: "a sound with no name in this cycle, or the last, or the one before"
  annotation "note_1771590801121_3", anchor: "An artifact-as-institution making a choice no living authority sanctioned", text: "The Pinnacle names the political crisis with admirable precision and stops exactly where it becomes dangerous. Qingfu'spire — which has never accepted the custody transfer, which would treat an unauthorized blessing of an exiled smuggler as provocation requiring formal response — does not appear. Not in Xi's account. Not in the Pinnacle's. Not even in Ingjeizhi's indifferent catalogue of warm-thing politics. Three perspectives, zero mentions of the faction with the strongest grievance. One witness might forget. Three witnesses all forgetting the same absent threat suggests the omission is itself a political act. Whoever assembled these testimonies chose not to include what happened next.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771590801121_4", anchor: "Something answered.", text: "Foundation Depths, strata 8 and below. Impressions I have catalogued but cannot attribute to any known civilization. Pressure-patterns in crystal that predate penguin sapience by margins I lack the methodology to estimate. Ingjeizhi describes a circuit completing with something beneath the deep ice, and I note only that the spire's account is consistent with what I have observed in the archive and have not, until now, found corroborated by any other source.", type: :temporal, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771590801121_5", anchor: "one hundred twelve pressure-units", text: "Ingjeizhi measures Xi's arrival in pressure-units. Not identity, not faction, not the moral weight of a smuggler entering a sacred space. Weight redistribution across cracked flooring. I find this the most honest account of the three — not because crystal is objective, but because it lacks the capacity for self-justification.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771590801121_6", anchor: "Xi set down a single fire-core. Wrapped in stolen Aurora Stack cloth.", text: "After three conflicting testimonies about cosmic frequencies and political calculation — a penguin leaves a fire-core on the floor for no one. The stolen cloth wrapping it carries more narrative freight than the entire Pinnacle delegation report. Whoever wrote this coda knew exactly what they were doing, placing it outside all three accounts, belonging to none of them. I would like to know who.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
